    <GaugingStation location="Muiresk" name="Deveron" number="9002">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station, the most downstream on the Deveron, draining mountainous headwaters.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Cableway rated, natural control. Lots of out of bank flow. Bypassing occurs on lb above about 3.2m; floodplain flows have been measured. Reasonably fitted rating derived from current meter gaugings, simple extrapolation beyond. Peak flow rating was revised in 1999 and a new single rating was judged to be suitable for the whole period of record. Rating revised in 2016.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station, about 38m wide.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in April 2017 (WINFAP Files v5). Chart data between 1960 &amp; 1987 was digitised in 2016.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural regime. Water abstraction point immediately d/s; no visible effect on level records.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Mountainous headwaters, often snowy in winter. Complex granite and older basic intrusives with Dalradian metamorphics. Some ORS. Mostly impermeable bedrock, &gt;80% overlain by superficial deposits. Some high moorland, mainly pastoral and arable; forestry. Minimal floodplains, mostly downstream. No significant catchment changes known.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Bypassing and scatter in gaugings above QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
